        <ezobject:attribute xmlns:ezremote="http://ez.no/ezobject" ezremote:id="2352" ezremote:identifier="intro" name="Intro" type="ezxmltext">
          <section xmlns:image="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/image/" xmlns:xhtml="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/xhtml/" xmlns:custom="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/custom/">
            <paragraph>Two-factor sign-in, passkeys, a Content Security Policy that blocks injected scripts and a "verify it's you" step for sensitive changes.</paragraph>
          </section>
        </ezobject:attribute>
        <ezobject:attribute xmlns:ezremote="http://ez.no/ezobject" ezremote:id="2353" ezremote:identifier="body" name="Body" type="ezxmltext">
          <section xmlns:image="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/image/" xmlns:xhtml="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/xhtml/" xmlns:custom="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/custom/">
            <section>
              <section>
                <header>Accounts that stay yours</header>
                <paragraph>Exponential 6.0.15 supports passkeys and time-based one-time passwords for every account, and asks editors to verify it's them again before they change a password, an email address or a security setting.</paragraph>
              </section>
              <section>
                <header>Defense in depth</header>
                <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/">
                  <ul>
                    <li>
                      <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/">Designs that run under a strict Content Security Policy: no inline scripts or styles.</paragraph>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/">Form tokens on every form that changes data.</paragraph>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/">Roles and policies that limit each user to exactly what they need.</paragraph>
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </paragraph>
              </section>
            </section>
          </section>
